Last year's weather, the same old terrace;
The sun sinks west—when shall it return?

Helplessly the blossoms fall and go,
Familiar swallows come back, as of old;
Alone I linger on the scented path of the small garden."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "**Butterflies Love Flowers: I Lean on the High Tower**

I linger, leaning on the high tower, in the gentle breeze;
My gaze stretches to the far horizon where spring sorrow grows,
Dim and heavy, rising from the edge of the sky.

Amidst the green grass and misty light of the setting sun,
Silent, who understands my meaning as I lean on the railing?

I intend to act with unbridled wildness, seeking drunken bliss;
To raise a glass, to sing aloud—forced joy tastes bitter still.

My robe bands loosen day by day, yet I regret nothing at all;
For her sake, I willingly waste away through weariness and decline."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "**Butterfly in Love with Flower**
*By Liu Yong*

I linger, leaning against the high tower, as the breeze blows gently;
Extending my gaze to the far horizon, spring’s sorrow rises darkly from the sky.
Amidst the grassy hues and misty light of the fading sun,
In silence, who can understand the meaning behind my reliance on the railing?

I intend to cast aside restraint, seeking oblivion in drunkenness;
Facing wine and singing songs, I force myself to joy, yet it turns tasteless.
Though my belt grows loose bit by bit, I shall never repent;
For her sake, I willingly endure this withering away."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "I lean long on the tower, the wind a whisper thin;
I gaze to the far edge—spring sorrow, dim,
Rises from the rim of the world.

Grass fades in mist and the last of the light;
No one can read my silence, my railing-bound plight.

I vow to drink wild, to seek one drunken night,
To sing before the cup—yet forced joy is no delight.
My belt grows loose, yet I would not repent;
For her, I gladly wear myself away."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "I lean upon the high tower, a slender wind caressing;
Gazing far, the spring's sorrow rises dimly from the sky.
In fading light, grass and mist glow softly, dying—
Silent, who could know the heart behind this railing?

I resolve to be wild, to seek one deep and drugged oblivion;
Wine raised, song sung—yet forced joy turns to nothingness.
My belt grows loose, my frame grows thin, yet never shall I grieve;
For her I would wither to the bone, and count it sweet."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
