I plan a wild recklessness to drink myself drunk;
wine before me, song to sing—
forced merriment still tastes of nothing.
My belt loosens day by day, yet I never regret;
for her I waste away to pallor, and to lean."}

{"source": {"title": "静夜思", "author": "李白", "text": "床前明月光，疑是地上霜。
举头望明月，低头思故乡。"}, "translation": "Before my bed, the bright moonlight gleams;
I wonder if it's frost upon the ground.
I raise my head to gaze at the bright moon,
Then bow down low and think of home so fond."}

{"source": {"title": "鹿柴", "author": "王维", "text": "空山不见人，但闻人语响。
返景入深林，复照青苔上。"}, "translation": "Empty mountains, no one in sight;
Yet voices echo through the height.
Last light returns to deep forest glades,
And falls once more on mossy shades."}

{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "A morning rain has settled Wei's light dust;
The travelers' inn is green, the willows newly bright.
Come, friend, drain one more cup of wine before you go—
West of Yang Pass, no old friend meets your sight."}

{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "Morning rain at Weicheng dampens the light dust;
The inn's willows are fresh and green.
I urge you to drink one more cup of wine—
West of Yang Pass, there will be no old friends."}

{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "At Dawn in Wei City Before You Leave for Anxi

The morning rain has wet the dust in Wei;
Fresh green willows shade the inn where we stay.
I beg you, drink this cup of wine once more—
West of Yang Pass, no old friend awaits you there."}

{"source": {"title": "鹿柴", "author": "王维", "text": "空山不见人，但闻人语响。
返景入深林，复照青苔上。"}, "translation": "Deer Enclosure

Empty mountain, no one in sight;
Yet human voices echo and ring.
The setting sun’s light pierces the deep woods,
And once again falls upon the green moss."}

