{"source": {"title": "春望", "author": "杜甫", "text": "国破山河在，城春草木深。
感时花溅泪，恨别鸟惊心。
烽火连三月，家书抵万金。
白头搔更短，浑欲不胜簪。"}, "translation": "**Spring View**

The nation shattered, yet the mountains, rivers stand;
Spring fills the city, grass and trees grow deep.
Grieving the times, the flowers splash with tears;
Loathing parting, birds alarm the heart.
Beacon fires have blazed three months unceasing;
A letter from home is worth ten thousand gold.
White-haired, I scratch—and the strands grow shorter still,
So sparse they can no longer hold a hairpin."}

{"source": {"title": "春望", "author": "杜甫", "text": "国破山河在，城春草木深。
感时花溅泪，恨别鸟惊心。
烽火连三月，家书抵万金。
白头搔更短，浑欲不胜簪。"}, "translation": "Spring Prospect

The realm lies shattered, yet the hills and streams endure;
Spring visits the city—grass and trees grow thick, untamed.
Touched by these times, the flowers weep;
Grieved by parting, birds' cries wound the heart.
For three months the beacon fires have burned;
A letter from home is worth ten thousand gold.
I scratch my white hair thinner still—
Now too sparse to hold a single pin."}

{"source": {"title": "黄鹤楼送孟浩然之广陵", "author": "李白", "text": "故人西辞黄鹤楼，烟花三月下扬州。
孤帆远影碧空尽，唯见长江天际流。"}, "translation": "My old friend bids farewell at Yellow Crane Tower, westward bound no more;
In the third month of blossoming mist he sails downstream to Yangzhou.
A lone sail, its shadow grows faint, swallowed by the boundless blue sky—
All I see is the Yangtze river flowing to the edge of the world."}

